<title>JAPAN: Japan May jobless rate matches record high 3.5 pct.</title>
<headline>Japan May jobless rate matches record high 3.5 pct.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-06-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's seasonally adjusted unemployment rate rose to 3.5 percent in May, up from 3.3 percent in April and matching the record high marked in May and June of 1996, the government's Management and Coordination Agency said on Friday.</p>
<p>But the jobs-to-applicants ratio for May was 0.73, up from 0.71 in the previous month, the Labour Ministry announced separately. This means there were 73 job openings for every 100 job seekers.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the jobs data:</p>
<p> (Adjusted)			     MAY	 APRIL     YEAR AGO</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		    3.5 pct   3.3 pct   3.5 pct</p>
<p> Jobs-to-applicants ratio	   0.73	0.71	0.69</p>
<p> (Unadjusted)			   MAY	 APRIL     YEAR AGO</p>
<p> Unemployment rate		    3.5 pct   3.4 pct   3.5 pct</p>
<p> Number of unemployed		 2.44 million  2.31 million  2.40 million</p>
<p>Number of employed</p>
<p>					   MAY	  YEAR/YEAR CHANGE</p>
<p> Overall				 66.32 million  +1.6 pct</p>
<p>Main Industries:</p>
<p>  Manufacturing			14.51 million  +1.0 pct</p>
<p>  Services			     16.65 million  +1.0 pct</p>
<p>  Wholesale, retail, restaurants 14.86 million  +4.1 pct</p>
<p>  Construction			  6.78 million  +5.1 pct</p>
<p>  Agriculture			   3.70 million  +2.2 pct</p>
</text>
